––– comment –––
Pool size N: shared=N sets it in the request that creates the pool. N is read as an integer, a
value that is not a number as 0, and clamped to 1..searchd threads - 2, so no N refuses a
document. A request that joins the open pool or commits it ignores its N.
––– input –––
source /tmp/shared.sh; sql "CREATE TABLE s_chunks (title TEXT, gid INT)"; gen s_chunks 1 3000 > /tmp/c1.ndjson; gen s_chunks 3001 6000 > /tmp/c2.ndjson; gen s_chunks 6001 9000 > /tmp/c3.ndjson; gen s_n 1 10 > /tmp/c0.ndjson; for n in 0 -1 abc 2x 100000; do sql "CREATE TABLE s_n (title TEXT, gid INT)"; post s_n "=$n" /tmp/c0.ndjson; leftovers s_n; commit s_n '' > /dev/null; sql "DROP TABLE s_n"; done
